Phase 12 introduces an explicit runtime validation boundary before controller and service logic.

Attach schemas to controller parameters
NestJS 12 route parameter decorators can carry Standard Schema metadata. The controller remains concise
because validation is declared where the data enters the handler.

import {
Body,
Controller,
Delete,
Get,
HttpCode,
HttpStatus,
Param,
Patch,
Post,
} from "@nestjs/common";
import { TasksService } from "./tasks.service";
import {
createTaskSchema,
CreateTaskDto,
taskIdSchema,
updateTaskSchema,
UpdateTaskDto,
} from "./tasks.schemas";

@Controller("tasks")
export class TasksController {
constructor(private readonly tasksService: TasksService) {}

@Post()
create(
@Body({ schema: createTaskSchema }) body: CreateTaskDto,
) {
return this.tasksService.create(body);
}

@Get()
findAll() {
return this.tasksService.findAll();
}

@Get(":id")
findOne(
@Param("id", { schema: taskIdSchema }) id: string,
) {
return this.tasksService.findOne(id);
}

@Patch(":id")
update(
@Param("id", { schema: taskIdSchema }) id: string,
@Body({ schema: updateTaskSchema }) body: UpdateTaskDto,
) {
return this.tasksService.update(id, body);
}

@Delete(":id")
@HttpCode(HttpStatus.NO_CONTENT)
async remove(
@Param("id", { schema: taskIdSchema }) id: string,
) {
await this.tasksService.remove(id);
}
}

Read the create route in English

@Post()
create(
@Body({ schema: createTaskSchema }) body: CreateTaskDto,
) {
return this.tasksService.create(body);
}

• @Post() maps POST /tasks.

• @Body(...) extracts the JSON body.

• schema: createTaskSchema attaches the runtime contract.

• the global StandardSchemaValidationPipe parses the value before the method runs.

• CreateTaskDto documents the validated output type at compile time.

• TasksService receives already validated request shape data.

Path parameters need validation too
HTTP path parameters arrive as strings. A malformed task identifier should be rejected before Prisma receives
a query for it.

@Get(":id")
findOne(
@Param("id", { schema: taskIdSchema }) id: string,
) {
return this.tasksService.findOne(id);
}

Figure 1 - Invalid UUID short-circuit
GET /tasks/not-a-uuid

↓

taskIdSchema fails

↓

400 Bad Request

↓

TasksService is not called

↓

Prisma is not queried

Validation reduces unnecessary database work and creates a clearer client error.

The service becomes simpler
The service no longer needs to defend against “title is a boolean” or “projectId is an object.” Its remaining
responsibilities are business/application behavior and persistence orchestration.

